14% more of product 1. Candidate 4 orders about 10% more of both, and candidate 0 about 19% more.\n- Accounting:\n  - A unit short costs 27 for product 0 (lost margin 8, minus the 12 not spent buying it, plus a 7 penalty) and 19 for product 1.\n  - Every unit ordered costs 12 (product 0) or 9 (product 1) whether or not it sells, because leftovers at the end are lost.\n  - Larger orders also raise the average carried stock, which adds holding cost.\n\n| Candidate | Product 0 cost | Product 1 cost | Total cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 5 | ≈ 15 700 | ≈ 6 500 | **≈ 22 200** |\n| 7 | ≈ 15 700 | ≈ 6 900 | ≈ 22 600 |\n| 4 | ≈ 16 200 | ≈ 6 700 | ≈ 22 900 |\n| 0 | ≈ 17 800 | ≈ 7 000 | ≈ 24 800 |\n\nFor product 0, candidates 5 and 7 tie. For product 1, extra stock beyond the forecast mostly spoils after one cycle. So candidate 7's extra 14% buys few avoided shortages and costs about 270 more in holding.\n\n**3. Risk when demand differs from forecast**\n- Around day 13 (demand 109), the arrival of both products plus leftover stock nears the 208-unit capacity, and any excess is lost.\n- The larger plans (0, then 4 and 7) are more likely to overflow. Candidate 5 is the safest here.\n- Shortages on days 1–3 can't be avoided under any plan, so they don't affect the comparison."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3894, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3894}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T01:59:12.873Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAmLprrnzQR17QpfX9ec"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "